    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Happy Path",
      "items": [
        "Browser sends an HTTP GET to the API",
        "API checks Redis before touching the database",
        "On a cache miss the API queries PostgreSQL"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Cache Fill",
      "items": [
        "After the DB returns rows the API writes them back to Redis",
        "The next identical request will be served from cache",
        "Cache fill is fire-and-forget — it does not block the response"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Why It Matters",
      "items": [
        "Redis absorbs read load and reduces DB pressure",
        "PostgreSQL is only hit on cold or expired keys",
        "The response path stays fast even on a miss"
